Alpha2OpenSdk — provenance and third-party notices
===================================================

This repository exists to keep the UBTECH Alpha2 robot usable now that UBTECH's
cloud services, developer portal, and app store are gone. The MIT license in the
LICENSE file applies to the original contributions described below.

Original contributions (MIT, (c) 2026 Dave Snowdon):
  - The SDK under ubtechalpha2robot/. It is an original reimplementation of the
    Alpha2 SDK interface, written from documented behaviour rather than copied from
    UBTECH's SDK. It removes the client-side store-authorization gate, adds
    conveniences such as chest_configureSonar, and uses corrected API names.
  - The developer documentation under docs/.
  - The example application(s) under examples/.

Interoperability with UBTECH's robot:
  - For an app to talk to the robot, certain interface-level facts must match what
    the robot's on-device software expects: AIDL interface/method names and order,
    service and broadcast action strings, serial command bytes, Serializable class
    shapes, and constant values. These facts are reproduced in this SDK because
    interoperability requires them; they originate from UBTECH's SDK/robot
    interface, in which UBTECH retains any applicable rights. No UBTECH source
    code, resources, model data, or grammar source is included here.

Third-party libraries:
  - None are bundled. The SDK depends only on the Android framework and the Java
    standard library.

The documentation was written from scratch and describes only factual/interface
information (API signatures, constant values, protocol behaviour) needed to
interoperate with the robot. Reverse-engineering and firmware-analysis notes that
informed this work are kept in a separate private archive, not in this repository.

If you are a rights holder and believe something here should be attributed
differently or removed, please open an issue.
